{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I understand you came in with right upper quadrant pain and vomiting. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. I’ve had Crohn’s for years and usually get pain on the left side, but this time it’s sharp and in the upper right, near my back. Started about five days ago after I ate a hamburger on vacation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’ve had nausea and vomiting—was it bile-colored?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, greenish. I’ve vomited a few times. I haven’t passed gas in days and my last bowel movement had blood in the toilet, not in the stool. That’s unusual—I’m usually loose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. Your history of multiple bowel surgeries makes us concerned about obstruction. You mentioned placing your own NG tube at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve done it before when I feel blocked. It helps. I did it again after the ED removed mine—didn’t know why they took it out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it in for now to help decompress your stomach. We’ve ordered blood work and a CT scan to check for obstruction or other causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m worried it’s another blockage. But this pain feels different—more constant and deeper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2192-03-23 05:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re looking into that. Given your history, we’re also checking liver and gallbladder, even though you’ve had your gallbladder out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2192-03-23 12:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray shows the NG tube is in place. We’re waiting on the CT results. Any change in pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2192-03-23 12:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still hurting, but the tube helps a little. I’m anxious—being in the hospital brings back bad memories."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2192-03-23 12:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ve noted your PTSD history. We’ll be cautious with medications. Let’s wait for the CT before increasing anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2192-03-23 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT scan is back. Good news—no bowel obstruction, no inflammation or perforation. But we see mild fatty liver and a stable adrenal nodule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2192-03-23 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No blockage? But I feel blocked. My belly is distended and I haven’t moved my bowels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2192-03-23 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The scan shows gas in the colon, but no mechanical obstruction. It might be a functional slowdown—common in Crohn’s with adhesions. We’ll keep the NG tube and start bowel stimulants."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2192-03-23 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Can I try coffee? It’s helped before with motility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2192-03-23 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can try a small amount once we confirm your electrolytes are stable. We’re also checking for infection—your labs show no signs of inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2192-03-23 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your abdominal X-ray shows dilated bowel loops, likely due to a known stricture. But no free air, so no perforation. We’ll give an enema to help with constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2192-03-23 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. The pain is still bad. Can I have something stronger for pain? I know I’ve had Dilaudid before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2192-03-23 21:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can give IV Dilaudid, but we need to be cautious. You’re on Valium at home, and combining them increases sedation risk. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2192-03-23 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand. But the pain is overwhelming. I trust you to keep me safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2192-03-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You passed stool last night after the enema and coffee. That’s progress. Your pain seems a bit better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2192-03-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, a little. But I still need pain meds. Can I have the Dilaudid again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2192-03-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave a dose last night. We’re concerned because your oxygen dipped briefly after—likely due to the combination with Valium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2192-03-24 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember—I felt like I stopped breathing for a second. That scared me. It brought back trauma from a past hospital stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2192-03-24 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A rapid response was called, and you responded well to Narcan. No lasting effects. But we need to be very careful. We’ll adjust your pain plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2192-03-24 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. But I still hurt. What are my options?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2192-03-24 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue low-dose Dilaudid with longer intervals and avoid Valium for now. We’ve also consulted your gastroenterologist and surgeon—they agree with our approach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2192-03-24 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat chest X-ray shows no pneumonia or fluid. The hypoxia was likely due to sedation, not aspiration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2192-03-24 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried I’d damaged my lungs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2192-03-24 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also watching your EKG. You were on cipro and Zofran, which can prolong the QT interval. Your QT was over 550, so we gave IV magnesium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2192-03-24 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. It runs in my family. Is it better now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2192-03-24 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s improved to about 440. We’ve stopped the QT-prolonging meds. Please follow up with an EKG as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2192-03-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. You passed gas, your abdomen is less distended, and you’re tolerating sips. We’ll try advancing your diet slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2192-03-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Can we remove the NG tube soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2192-03-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll try a trial without it today. If you don’t vomit and keep food down, we can remove it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2192-03-25 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great job—you kept the liquids down. We’re removing the NG tube. How’s the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2192-03-25 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still there, but manageable. What about pain meds at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2192-03-25 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll prescribe oral Dilaudid 4 mg every six hours as needed. But no Tramadol—you should avoid it. We’ve coordinated with your PCP and gastroenterologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2192-03-25 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember—Dr. ___ said it could trigger seizures with my history. Thank you for checking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2192-03-25 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll also continue your gabapentin and other home meds. Your urine had blood initially, but it’s cleared. Still, follow up with a repeat urinalysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2192-03-25 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my iron? I’ve been anemic before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2192-03-25 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin dropped to 9.6, but it’s above your baseline. Continue your iron and vitamin B12. Check labs at your next visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home today. You’re walking well, eating, and pain is controlled with oral meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. Can my husband come in? I want him to hear the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. We’ll go over everything. You’re on Dilaudid for pain, but use it sparingly. Avoid driving. Continue all other medications, including fondaparinux for your stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Follow up with your gastroenterologist and PCP. Get an EKG soon and repeat urinalysis. If pain worsens or you can’t keep food down, return immediately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel anxious or PTSD symptoms flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Contact your mental health provider. We’ve noted your needs—social work can help coordinate. You’re strong, and we’re here to support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I’m grateful for your care and patience."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I worry about the adrenal nodule?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s stable and likely benign. Your endocrinologist can monitor it. No action needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the liver? The ultrasound said fatty liver."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mild steatosis. Continue healthy diet and avoid alcohol. It’s common and often stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my spleen is enlarged?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mild splenomegaly, likely from chronic inflammation. No intervention needed, but your doctor will keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for explaining everything so clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. We’re glad you’re feeling better. Discharge papers are ready—nurse will go over them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to follow up with all my doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2192-03-26 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best plan. Take care, and feel better soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2192-03-23 04:26:00",
    "admission_end": "2192-03-26 16:16:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex history of Crohn’s disease, short gut syndrome, and multiple prior bowel surgeries was admitted for acute right upper quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and constipation, concerning for small bowel obstruction. Imaging showed no mechanical obstruction, colitis, or perforation, but revealed mild hepatic steatosis and stable findings. She self-placed an NG tube for symptomatic relief. During hospitalization, she experienced transient apnea after receiving IV Dilaudid and Valium, requiring Narcan reversal, which was managed without complications. Pain was eventually controlled with cautious opioid use and bowel regimen including enemas and coffee. Her symptoms improved with conservative management, and she was discharged home on oral hydromorphone for pain, with follow-up plans for EKG monitoring due to QT prolongation, repeat urinalysis for resolved hematuria, and coordination with her outpatient providers.",
    "problems": [
      "Crohn's disease, unspecified, with intestinal obstruction",
      "Apnea, not elsewhere classified",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Chronic pain syndrome",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Long term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Acquired absence of other specified parts of digestive tract",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Gross hematuria",
      "Post-traumatic stress disorder, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
